@weizijun I think this might be a bit simpler approach. As a side benefit we can now create a TSDB index with a much simpler command:
```
PUT test
{
  "settings": {
    "index.mode": "time_series",
    "index.routing_path": "dim"
  },
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "dim": {
        "type": "keyword",
        "time_series_dimension": true
      },
      "val": {
        "type": "double"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

> @weizijun I think this might be a bit simpler approach. As a side benefit we can now create a TSDB index with a much simpler command:
> 
> ```
> PUT test
> {
>   "settings": {
>     "index.mode": "time_series",
>     "index.routing_path": "dim"
>   },
>   "mappings": {
>     "properties": {
>       "dim": {
>         "type": "keyword",
>         "time_series_dimension": true
>       },
>       "val": {
>         "type": "double"
>       }
>     }
>   }
> }
> ```

It means that   `index.time_series.start_time` and `index.time_series.end_time` are not the required settings in the tsdb index.
In the previous design, the two settings must configured in the tsdb index. Maybe discuss with @nik9000  and @martijnvg.

